All quantities condition on convergence and their stated domain. No minimum or score certification.
Magnitude imbalance M=abs(a)-abs(b) is distinct from signed D; neither is a score share.
C_magnitude normalizes magnitude imbalance on all valid-reference nonzero pairs, regardless of polarity.
C_bounded requires nonnegative oriented block means; opposite-sign cases remain in D.
MCSE uses independent replications within each cell. Formats are not pooled.
Magnitude selection is abs(M)>.1; first means M>.1, second M<-.1. Conditional proportions use selected counts, not n_finite.
Conditional selection MCSE is the nominal per-cell binomial SE. Pooled heterogeneous-cell bars require their own uncertainty calculation.
